HYPOTHESIS H1b  [paradigm: P1_ashby]  (seq 2)
======================================================================
CLAIM      : The BLIND advantage is not an artifact of assuming a BLIND report always fixes the blind spot. It survives a hostile parameterisation where BLIND only leads to a structural fix 20% of the time.
PREDICTION : C_hostile still beats A_baseline on undetected_ticks.
FALSIFIER  : FALSIFIED if C_hostile reduces undetected_ticks by less than 15% vs A_baseline, or the CI spans zero. That would mean the H1 result was an artifact of the cure assumption.
METRIC     : undetected_ticks  (lower_better, min effect 0.15)
ARMS       : C_hostile (treatment) vs A_baseline (control)
